paseo-seamless-claude-accounts 1.7.0 (9db99b1), for two organizations of one person.

- A switch moves only the Claude login and its organization's trusted device token. The
  rest of a credential file stays with its config dir: MCP servers' OAuth logins (their
  refresh tokens rotate, so a copy would break one of them) and the client registrations
  and plugin secrets, which a new dir copies from the live one.
- When Anthropic can't be asked, the account block chooses between two organizations of
  one person only if the last owner recorded for the seat agrees. Settings naming the
  other organization are corrected at the next sync.
- Claude Code's credit and budget notices count as limits. A notice must end after
  "limit" or go on with "·", "|", "—" or "(", so ordinary replies don't match.

